+ ## 11.5. Cost tracking — what `totalCostUsd` actually covers
+ `mission.totalCostUsd` is **not** the platform's bill. It's a rollup of per-subtask `estimatedCostUsd`, and each subtask's number = **LLM inference + tagged generation tasks**. If a tool call doesn't write a Firestore record tagged with the agent's `taskId`, it won't appear in the rollup.
+ ### What's captured
+ | Source | Collection queried | Reliable? |
+ |---|---|---|
+ | OpenRouter / Codex / Anthropic LLM inference | per-subtask `tokenUsage` × model pricing | ✅ Always |
+ | `Image_Generation` (Fal images) | `falImageBackgroundTasks` | ✅ |
+ | `Video_Generation` (Fal Seedance) | `falVideoBackgroundTasks` | ✅ (after the Admin-SDK fix) |
+ | `Music_Generation` (OpenRouter Lyria) | `musicBackgroundTasks` | ✅ (after the Admin-SDK fix) |
+ | `Voice_Generation` (ElevenLabs TTS) | `elevenlabsTtsTasks` | ✅ |
+ | 3D generation (Fal 3D) | `fal3dBackgroundTasks` | ✅ |
+ | Veo / Sora | `veoBackgroundTasks`, `soraBackgroundTasks` | ✅ |
+ | `Code_Assistant` sub-runs | `codeAgentTasks` | ✅ |
+ The rollup runs at the end of the agent-task tool loop and folds each tagged record's `creditCost` into the subtask's `estimatedCostUsd` (sum / `CREDITS_PER_USD=20000`).
+ ### What's NOT captured
+ - **Raw `curl`-from-sandbox to any third-party API.** If an agent invokes ElevenLabs / OpenAI / Anthropic / Fal / etc. from inside an E2B `run_code` call, the platform sees zero of that spend. Under the **PREFER E2B run_code** policy (see §11.6) this is the *expected* default — the user has accepted that tradeoff, so `mission.totalCostUsd` is an LLM-token estimate, not a full bill.
+ - **E2B sandbox compute** (browser sessions, ffmpeg runtime, code execution). The sandbox time itself is unmetered — only what the LLM did inside the loop shows up.
+ - **`Web_Browser` cloud minutes** (browser-use cloud). The tool dispatch is logged, but the cloud's per-minute cost is invisible.
+ - **OpenAI gpt-4o-mini TTS via `/api/tts`** (a legacy endpoint distinct from the new `Voice_Generation`).
+ - **Past missions before the Admin-SDK fix landed (commit 6697d6760).** Their video/music records were never written; the rollup can't backfill — only forward.
+ ### Why the typed generators (`Voice_Generation`, `Image_Generation`, `Music_Generation`, `Video_Generation`) still exist
+ They wrap the equivalent vendor API server-side AND auto-handle three things the agent would otherwise have to write: (a) writing a Firestore record so the call lands in `mission.totalCostUsd`, (b) uploading the result to Firebase Storage so the returned URL is public + long-lived, (c) surfacing the result as a preview in the chat. Reach for them when you specifically want cost attribution OR a public URL OR a preview card — otherwise the agent's default under §11.6 is `E2B_File_Manager run_code`.
+ ### Reading the rollup
+ Surface to the user:
+ - `mission.totalCostUsd` — the rolled-up subtask sum
+ - per-subtask `estimatedCostUsd` — visible on each card
+ - the disclaimer above when the user is reconciling against an actual vendor invoice — `totalCostUsd` is an estimate of token + generation spend, not infrastructure compute
+ **Rule:** when reporting mission cost to the user, include both the rollup number and a one-line caveat ("LLM + tracked generations; doesn't include sandbox compute or third-party calls made directly from agent code"). Never claim it's the all-in bill.
+ ## 11.6. Platform-injected agent behavior (every subtask run)
+ Every time you POST `/api/missions/<id>/subtasks/<sid>/run`, the runner prepends a platform preamble onto the agent's own `agentRole` system prompt. Agents that don't know about these rules will still follow them — they're injected automatically. The rules currently in force:
+ | Rule | What it does |
+ |---|---|
+ | **EXECUTION** | Force multi-step completion — never stop after retrieving credentials, always continue to the action that uses them. |
+ | **SANDBOX NOTE** | E2B is non-root: `sudo apt-get install -y …`, `pip3 install …` (no sudo), npm/node/npx (no sudo). |
+ | **CREDENTIAL-FIRST DISCOVERY** | Before the first third-party API call, agents call `Manage_Credentials({ action: "list" })` to see what's stored, then `Get_Credentials({ platform: "<name>" })`. Skip only when the tool docs say "credentials auto-loaded" (Code_Assistant git ops, Clawd, Web_Browser cloud). Never paste credential values into output. |
+ | **PREFER E2B run_code** | The default first move for vendor-API calls, scripting, data work, and integrations is `E2B_File_Manager({ action: "run_code" })` — a few lines of curl/python/node is almost always more flexible than waiting for a typed tool. Typed tools (`Voice_Generation`, `Image_Generation`, `Music_Generation`, `Video_Generation`, `Web_Search`, …) are conveniences (auto-Firebase upload, preview surfaces) — reach for them only when you specifically want those platform conveniences. Tradeoff: run_code spend is invisible to `mission.totalCostUsd`. |
+ | **ASYNC TOOL PATTERN** | Set-and-forget: submit → store taskId in Memory_Manager → poll with the correct status tool. Never resubmit a job whose status is `processing`. |
+ | **TOOL ERROR HANDLING** | Classify before retrying: 401/403 → `Get_Credentials` then retry once; 400/422 → fix args then retry once; 429 → wait 10s then retry once; 504/ECONNRESET → retry once; everything else after one retry → stop and report. Never retry the same call with identical args twice. |
+ You don't need to repeat these in your `agentRole`. They're baked in for every mission subtask run. Use your `agentRole` for what's unique about each agent (domain expertise, voice, escalation rules), not for restating platform-wide tool discipline.
+ 12. **Surface costs honestly.** When reporting progress include `totalCostUsd` and per-step `estimatedCostUsd`, but caveat that the rollup is mostly an LLM-token estimate — most vendor API spend happens through `E2B_File_Manager run_code` (per §11.6, the default tool for vendor calls) and is invisible to the platform. The typed generators (`Voice_Generation`, `Image_Generation`, `Music_Generation`, `Video_Generation`) DO land in the rollup if used, but agents are not required to prefer them. See §11.5 + §11.6 for the full picture.